From 0b26c75af3abbfc0f7cfc6c93efe72061141d46c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:41:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: read-only App security & privacy page

Port of the GrapheneOS-era UI5B Application Security & Privacy page.
One read-only page per app in its own user; every row names its
evidence class (DECLARED, ENFORCED, OBSERVED, INFERRED, UNKNOWN):

* identity and provenance: package, version, SDK, installer chain,
  signing certificate SHA-256 and rotation, install type, build flags;
* effective access per sensitive group, from the same evaluator as
  the All apps row (allowed, approximate, limited, not allowed,
  unknown), with a hand-off to the platform App permissions page;
* components: activities, services, receivers and providers (total,
  enabled, exported, exported without a permission, first names),
  instrumentation and powerful bindings (accessibility, notification
  listener, VPN, input method, autofill, device admin);
* code: packaged native libraries and ABIs from a bounded scan of the
  installed APK entry names (UNKNOWN if nothing could be read, "at
  least" when a bound is hit), shared libraries; tracker signatures
  UNKNOWN (no dataset is installed);
* network and background: network state from the same policy as
  Network access (link to it), battery optimization, stopped state;
  destinations UNKNOWN;
* history: first install and last update; permission history UNKNOWN.

Entries: App info > App security & privacy, and Settings > Apps > App
security & privacy (a list with the sensitive-access summary).
Exported as org.sableos.settings.APP_SECURITY for Sable Tools (action
alone); a package: URI opens that app's page. Nothing is changed by
the page; everything is read off the main thread.
